# Build and test with `bd`

Always use the project-root [`bd`](bd) script for configuring, building, and running tests. Do not invoke `cmake`, `make`, `ninja`, or `ctest` directly (including under `build/`).

```bash
# ✅ GOOD
./bd build
./bd test
./bd all
./bd build -j2
./bd test --config Release -j16

# ❌ BAD
cmake --build build -j$(nproc)
make -C build effects-tests
ctest --test-dir build
./build/tests/effects-tests "[movement]"
```

## Failure handling

If `bd` fails (configure, build, or test), **stop and report the failure to the user**. Do not retry with another build system, a different generator, or ad-hoc compile/link commands. Fix source/config issues and re-run `bd` only when that is the clear fix.

## Parallelism

Prefer `bd`'s default job count (from MemTotal) unless the user asks for `-j` / `--jobs` or `BD_JOBS`.
